.TH EPOLL_WAIT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
epoll_wait \- Linux x86-64 syscall 232
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int epoll_wait(int epoll, void* events, int maximum, int timeout);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits for events. Each Linux x86-64 kernel event is 12 bytes: a 32-bit event mask followed by eight data bytes; the data is unaligned.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR epoll_wait (2)
